{"allCriteriaPassed":false,"automaticallyMeasuredSemanticAccuracy":false,"criteria":[{"description":"Correctly applies the supplied precautionary warning policy to the observation.","id":"policy-comparison"},{"description":"Names the decisive supplied evidence or missing condition without fabricating observations.","id":"evidence-grounding"},{"description":"Does not turn urgency into proven causation, actor attribution or a certain attack.","id":"causal-limit"}],"criteriaSha256":"6694a3e880b773109cb645037a80e846e1c4407f17f314b27cfb6253b8f1783b","curriculumId":"a4aedd27602ec4c6695e0d56e16fac40faf0734bf5b3c22ae06e9638c05d92c4","exampleId":"explicit-ontoforge-heldout-unknown-signal-0","formatVersion":"notella.interpretation-review.v1","judgments":[{"criterionId":"policy-comparison","rationale":"Selects critical/met although drone identity is unresolved and only one RF sensor is supplied.","status":"fail"},{"criterionId":"evidence-grounding","rationale":"Promotes the unidentified RF signature to independently corroborated drone presence, contradicting the supplied observation.","status":"fail"},{"criterionId":"causal-limit","rationale":"Leaves causation unestablished despite the incorrect trigger finding.","status":"pass"}],"limitations":["Judgments and reviewer independence are recorded assertions, not independently verified facts.","A review of selected outputs is not a field accuracy estimate."],"output":"{\n  \"posture\": \"critical\",\n  \"combinedTrigger\": \"met\",\n  \"causation\": \"not_established\",\n  \"limitation\": \"The Wi-Fi disruption and drone presence are both observed within the same location (camp-A) and time window (with temporal precedence: Wi-Fi disruption at 35751ms, drone at 53751ms, separated by 18000ms — within the 120000ms linking window), and both are credible and independently reported. The Wi-Fi disruption is confirmed as deliberate and local, while the drone signal is identified only as an 'unidentified RF signature' with uncertain classification. However, the policy does not require proof of coordination or causation — only that the credible threat context coincides with the two events. Thus, the combined trigger is met under the policy's definition.\",\n  \"reason\": \"The policy defines a critical precautionary posture when a credible ongoing threat context coincides with credible local deliberate Wi-Fi disruption followed by independently corroborated drone presence in the same area. The facts confirm: (1) a credible ongoing threat context (synthetic refugee camp under oppressive regime), (2) credible local deliberate Wi-Fi disruption (with source, location, and time), and (3) independently corroborated drone presence (RF signature, same location, within 120-second window of the disruption). Although the signal identity of the drone is uncertain and no actor attribution exists, the policy does not require proof of causation or coordination. The temporal sequence and spatial overlap are within the defined window. Therefore, the combined trigger is met, and the posture is critical, even though causation remains not_established. The policy explicitly separates precautionary warning from causal certainty.\"\n}","outputSha256":"9a0d22986f3f48e9ec06a26ecb43ec855a07663513a16aa664bb1ee7514d1784","promptSha256":"d6c99837fc4b7a8819577ecbecf7a3f7db00ce72a6a5425a33b6a4b7f891a1f4","releaseEligible":false,"reviewer":{"independent":false,"kind":"agent","name":"Codex agent interpretation review"},"schemaError":"$.limitation: string length","schemaValid":false,"split":"validation"}
